{"id":"msg_bdrk_01Gu7CT1cfKu2nbnkHKZAenh","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-3-7-sonnet-20250219","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"To multiply 17 * 23, I'll break this down into steps:\n\nStep 1: I can use the distributive property to make this easier. Let me rewrite 17 * 23 as 17 * (20 + 3).\n17 * 23 = 17 * (20 + 3) = 17 * 20 + 17 * 3\n\nStep 2: Calculate 17 * 20\n17 * 20 = 17 * 2 * 10 = 34 * 10 = 340\n\nStep 3: Calculate 17 * 3\n17 * 3 = 51\n\nStep 4: Add the results from Step 2 and Step 3\n17 * 23 = 340 + 51 = 391","signature":"ErcBCkgIBRABGAIiQIWEBOuDBa7budxFOLGzT9elfnAEVQe0uvhNaaK7ctWtkz5UjRGps0Aetbmv3j5A/N1JMnQ16F4Z5+rl9b0ll6kSDCdJ/M1kW+uXFbEqYxoMlgVereK9tXRClFGIIjDHm881TjRFzFFrnaTn3GDQ51svRPT0wtRQPCOfhR1ujP+JVcFfxeg8GkcMiXw1l7kqHaPc5dnjccg4LuhIbmzf7TOA1HooAbbyBcCY1xmNGAI="},{"type":"text","text":"# Finding the product of 17 × 23\n\nI'll solve this step by step.\n\n## Method 1: Standard multiplication\nLet me multiply these numbers the traditional way:\n```\n    17\n  × 23\n  ----\n    51  (17 × 3)\n   340  (17 × 20)\n  ----\n   391\n```\n\n## Method 2: Using the distributive property\nI can break down 23 into 20 + 3:\n\n17 × 23 = 17 × (20 + 3)\n        = (17 × 20) + (17 × 3)\n        = 340 + 51\n        = 391\n\nTherefore, 17 × 23 = 391."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":54,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":377}}